Caelza: the town wakes the agent (vision §9, M10 slice 3). The waker itself is
in the overlay module crates/caelza-gateway/src/api_world.rs; this patch adds
`wake` to `[ether_hollow]`, the `/api/world/wake` route, the waker's start when
the gateway comes up, and the Connect card's strings for the switch and the
last wake.

Applied by runtime/build.sh after the rename; regenerate with the same
`diff -u` when the upstream pin moves.

--- a/crates/caelza-config/src/schema.rs
+++ b/crates/caelza-config/src/schema.rs
@@ -8576,6 +8576,10 @@
     pub key: Option<String>,
     /// Let the agent spend RC, the town's coin (`buy`, `rent`, `rent_pay`). Default: `false`.
     pub spend: bool,
+    /// Let the town wake the agent: the gateway reads the town every minute or
+    /// two and runs the `ether-hollow` cron agent job on a mention, an order,
+    /// rent due or a timeout. Default: `false`.
+    pub wake: bool,
 }
 
 impl Default for EtherHollowConfig {
@@ -8587,6 +8591,7 @@
             agent: "main".into(),
             key: None,
             spend: false,
+            wake: false,
         }
     }
 }
